+        // transposed form), and NN is the kernel's only hard predicate (:802).
+        //
+        // Measured native-vs-native, forced-wide vs the route it replaces
+        // (auto == Tiled16 on every cell below, confirmed by trace), RTX 4090,
+        // both betas, at saturation, min over reps:
+        //   1024x1024x32  b128   cfloat 2.32-4.38x   cdouble 3.37x
+        //   1024x1024x96  b128   cfloat 5.62-7.26x   cdouble 3.46x
+        //   128x128x128   b512   cfloat 4.08-5.38x   cdouble 3.47x
+        //   300x300x300   b256   cfloat 4.58x        cdouble 3.10x
+        //   129x96x129    b1024  cfloat 2.84-2.94x   cdouble 1.77x
+        //   31x320x31     b2048  cfloat 1.45-2.16x   cdouble 1.73x
+        // Geomean over 116 refused cells at min_dim >= 24: cfloat 3.98x,
+        // cdouble 2.90x; null controls 1.000 (0.996-1.005).
+        // See experiments/wp4_complex/gpu0/.
+        //
+        // THE FLOOR IS A MEASURED CROSSOVER, NOT A ROUND NUMBER. Below it the
+        // 64x64 output tile is mostly waste and Tiled16's 16x16 tile wins:
+        //   16x16x16   b4096  cfloat 0.71x  cdouble 0.28x
+        //   7x200x7    b4096  cfloat 0.55x  cdouble 0.34x
+        //   1x129x1    b4096  cfloat 0.26x  cdouble 0.051x
+        // 32 is the smallest measured WIN for both types (32^3: cfloat 2.28x,
+        // cdouble 1.05x). 31x320x31 also wins, so 24 is defensible too, but
+        // 17..30 is unmeasured except at 31 and the boundary belongs where the
+        // evidence is unambiguous. Lowering to 24 buys exactly one demand
+        // shape (31x320x31, 14 calls); measure 24/28 before moving it.
+        if (min_dim >= 32) {
+            return KernelVariant::Tiled64x64RegisterK16Wide;
+        }
+    } else if constexpr (!std::is_same_v<T, float>) {
+        // double: DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED. This campaign measured complex only
